{"text": "So pull back. Out of the silicon wells, where photons became electrons. Up through the colour filters. Back through the glass that folded a telephoto lens into a sliver, past the sensor floating on its magnets. Out through the sapphire, and back to the thing in your hand. One tap. A beam folded four times. A sensor steadied thousands of times a second. Tens of millions of buckets counted. And billions of calculations, all in about the time it takes you to blink. That big lens still wins on raw light. Nothing this thin can match that much glass. But the phone found a second answer to the same problem. The lens beats the dark with size. The phone beats it with speed, and mathematics. That's one camera. There's a lot more hardware hiding in plain sight. So tell me in the comments: what should we take apart next? This is Deep Teardown. I'll see you inside the next one.", "alignment": {"characters": ["S", "o", " ", "p", "u", "l", "l", " ", "b", "a", "c", "k", ".", " ", "O", "u", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "i", "l", "i", "c", "o", "n", " ", "w", "e", "l", "l", "s", ",", " ", "w", "h", "e", "r", "e", " ", "p", "h", "o", "t", "o", "n", "s", " ", "b", "e", "c", "a", "m", "e", " ", "e", "l", "e", "c", "t", "r", "o", "n", "s", ".", " ", "U", "p", " ", "t", "h", "r", "o", "u", "g", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "o", "l", "o", "u", "r", " ", "f", "i", "l", "t", "e", "r", "s", ".", " ", "B", "a", "c", "k", " ", "t", "h", "r", "o", "u", "g", "h", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "g", "l", "a", "s", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "f", "o", "l", "d", "e", "d", " ", "a", " ", "t", "e", "l", "e", "p", "h", "o", "t", "o", " ", "l", "e", "n", "s", " ", "i", "n", "t", "o", " ", "a", " ", "s", "l", "i", "v", "e", "r", ",", " ", "p", "a", "s", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "s", "e", "n", "s", "o", "r", " ", "f", "l", "o", "a", "t", "i", "n", "g", " ", "o", "n", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "m", "a", "g", "n", "e", "t", "s", ".", " ", "O", "u", "t", " ", "t", "